# What never belongs in a Docker build context.
#
# There was no such file until now, and two things followed from that.
#
# **Secrets were baked into the image.** `COPY apps/api/ apps/api/` copied
# `apps/api/.env` — the admin password, the database password, the messaging
# token — into a layer, where it stayed for the life of the image. Anyone who
# could read the image could read them.
#
# It also broke config in a way that took an afternoon to trace: the API loads
# `.env` with dotenv, real environment variables win over it, and Compose only
# sets variables the *current* `.env` names. A key dropped from the live file
# but still present-and-empty in the baked one therefore came back as an empty
# string — which fails `min(1)` where absent would have passed — and the error
# named a variable that was not in the file anybody was looking at.
#
# Rebuild after adding this, and rotate anything that was in a published image.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.gitignore

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs. Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in only invites a stale
# `dist` shadowing a fresh compile.
dist
**/dist
apps/api/dist
packages/shared/dist

# The Flutter apps are not part of the API image, and their build directories
# hold hundreds of megabytes — including release APKs. Sending those to the
# daemon on every build is why the context takes so long to upload on a 1 GiB
# box with no memory to spare.
apps/mobile
apps/partner

# The web app is deployed on Vercel, not here.
apps/web/dist
apps/web/node_modules

# Local-only.
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
coverage
**/coverage
